Consider a closed spherical surface $S$ on which the outward-pointing surface element is $d\mathbf{S} = \hat{\mathbf{r}}\, dS$, where $\hat{\mathbf{r}}$ is the radial unit vector and $dS$ is the scalar area element. Using the result $\nabla\phi \cdot \hat{\mathbf{r}} = \frac{\partial\phi}{\partial r}$, show that

$$\nabla\phi \cdot d\mathbf{S} = \frac{\partial\phi}{\partial r}\, dS$$

